cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SigmaPro: estadística para la investigación agronómica y biológica"
abstract: >-
  SigmaPro is a self-contained web application for the statistical analysis of agronomic and
  biological research, entirely in the browser, with no installation and no server-side
  computation; the data never leave the computer. It covers experimental designs (completely
  randomized, randomized complete blocks, Latin square, split plots, split-split plots, strip
  plots, balanced incomplete blocks and lattices) with mean comparisons, contrasts and orthogonal
  polynomials; assumption checking; t and nonparametric tests; ANCOVA, regression, correlation and
  contingency tables; linear mixed models, repeated measures, variance components and
  heritability; generalized linear and generalized linear mixed models; nonlinear regression;
  response surfaces, mixtures and desirability; multi-environment trials with stability, AMMI and
  GGE; sample size and power, sampling, survival, time series and multivariate analysis (78
  analyses). A guided assistant and a visual model builder lead to each analysis, whose report
  explains the conclusion in words, with publication tables and figures, a methods paragraph and
  the equivalent R code. Each analysis has a theory sheet with its model and hypotheses, its
  assumptions and how to check them, the data it needs with templates, how to read the output
  and its references. Bilingual interface (Spanish and English). Every method was checked against
  R, number by number.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Luis Ángel"
    family-names: "Barrera-Guzmán"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8057-2583"
